Reference quirk.

`vid` marks a paragraph that continues a verse begun earlier. The paragraph
after the table starts verse 3 itself (`\p` newline `\v 3`), after verse
2-7 ended inside the table, so it continues nothing; the usfm-js reference
gives it `vid="TIT 1:3"` anyway. Every other paragraph in the file that
starts with a verse has no `vid`.

--- origin.xml
+++ origin.xml
@@ -34,7 +34,7 @@
       <cell style="tcr3" align="end">54,400<verse eid="TIT 1:2-7" /></cell>
     </row>
   </table>
-  <para style="p" vid="TIT 1:3">
+  <para style="p">
     <verse number="3" style="v" sid="TIT 1:3" />At the right time, he revealed his word by the message that he trusted me to deliver, by the command of God our savior.<verse eid="TIT 1:3" /></para>
   <para style="s5" />
   <para style="p">
